# Drafted by Gemini (R21 understudy), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Tarnished bells jingle on the frayed points of this jester's cap, and greasepaint sits thick in the creases of a face that has forgotten how to rest.
fd_understudy [angry]: Look at that painted bladder on the maypole, stealing my billing and my bows! I am Barnaby Tuppence, the one true Lord of Fools.
fd_understudy [sly]: That squeaking balloon is merely my understudy, grown swollen on cheap applause. Stand witness to my routine, travellers, and judge which of us wears the motley best!
* Be his judge -> accept
* Leave -> END

~ accept
fd_understudy [smile]: Splendid, a discerning house at last! Why did the grave-digger wed the baker's daughter? Because they both knew how to make a tidy crust rise!
quest chuckles_understudy asked
-> menu

~ menu
* Humour him. -> humour
* [Performance DC 15] Tell a better joke than his -> joke_ok | joke_fail
* [Insight DC 14] See what he really is -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [ends:chuckles_understudy] Tell him the truth: he is a man in a hat -> truth
* Leave -> END

~ humour
Narrator: At your applause, the glassy-eyed revellers nearby chime in right on the beat, giving the old trouper the clean, honest laugh he has chased for ages.
fd_understudy [smile]: You hear that timing, you overgrown turnip on a string? That is how a master holds the square! Take this purse, friends, with the Lord's compliments.
set understudy_outcome = "humoured"
quest chuckles_understudy done
gold +40
-> END

~ joke_ok
Narrator: His painted jaw drops, and then a rusty, startled bark of laughter shakes the little bells on his collar.
fd_understudy [smile]: Oh, that is dreadful, that is marvellous! I have not laughed since the bills went up in... well, never mind when. Take the prize, you earned the top spot!
set understudy_outcome = "outjoked"
quest chuckles_understudy done
gold +40
-> END

~ joke_fail
fd_understudy [sly]: All delivery and no punch, my dear amateurs! Leave the rib-tickling to the reigning monarch of mirth, and let us try from the top.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
Narrator: Beneath the cracked white paint is no fiend at all, only a bone-weary pantomime player whose boots are worn through from years of forced revelry. A gentle word about his craft makes his shoulders drop.
fd_understudy [weary]: A hall with footlights and a curtain that actually comes down... Lord above, I had nearly forgotten. Thank you for remembering a working player, friends, take this.
set understudy_outcome = "known"
quest chuckles_understudy done
gold +40
-> END

~ insight_fail
fd_understudy [smile]: Drink it in, good folk, the profile of a master! Notice how the bells catch the bonfire light when I take my bow.
-> menu

~ truth
Narrator: His smile goes brittle under the tallow paint, and he tugs his crooked points straight with stiff, trembling fingers.
fd_understudy [angry]: Philistines and hecklers, bought off by a bladder of hot wind! I shall take my act to the parade and show them what real stagecraft looks like!
set understudy_outcome = "slighted"
quest chuckles_understudy slighted
-> END
